The projection tower in the recursion immediately before Theorem 4.4 is anchored at a continuous-lattice projection j_0 from [D_0 → D_0] onto D_0, and the successor of level n is the function-space projection induced by the projection at level n. `towerProj.succ` says that successor has inclusion equal to conjugation by the inclusion and retraction of the previous level, and retraction equal to conjugation by the retraction and inclusion; both equalities are definitional. `towerProj.succ_incl_apply` says the successor inclusion acts by i_{n+1}(x)(y) = i_n(x(j_n(y))), and `towerProj.succ_retr_apply` says the successor retraction acts by j_{n+1}(x')(y) = j_n(x'(i_n(y))). Both are definitional. `towerProj.incl_apply` says application is preserved by the tower embeddings: the level-n embedding of f(x) equals the level-(n+1) embedding of f applied to the level-n embedding of x. The successor formula expands the right-hand side, and the retraction law cancels the retraction against the embedding.
